## WHAT ACTUALLY BLOCKED IT

**THE SUCCESSOR ROW, AND ITS COST IS THE IDENTIFICATION OF THE SEQUENCE AND NOT
THE STEP ARITHMETIC.** `[LJ-1.536]` split that row into three factors in
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/runs/Control536d.agda:135-148`; that file exhausted 8 GB
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/runs/ctld-0.time`), so no factor was measured in it. It
then reduced to `runs/Control536e.agda` and `runs/Control536f.agda`, which
carry **factor 1 alone**, and measured 425.73 s and 417.18 s
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/runs/ctle-0.time`, `runs/ctlf-0.time`). **It never
isolated factor 2**, and its conclusion "98 PERCENT OF THE COST IS `sucV`"
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md:248`) is a statement about factor 1
against factor 3 only. This task isolated all three: factor 1 is curable to
0.69 s (`runs/Control565a.agda`, `runs/ctla-0.time`), factor 3 is free at
1.75 s (`runs/Control565j.agda`, `runs/ctlj-0.out`), and **factor 2, one delta
step that identifies `seq α oα` with `hierL (sucV α) …`, exhausts 8 GB in
234.95 s** (`runs/Control565e.agda`, `runs/ctle-0.out`), while its twin with
the same spelling on both sides costs 1.71 s (`runs/Control565f.agda`,
`runs/ctlf-0.out`).

